# What NOT to publish.
#
# CAREFUL: npm reads ONLY this file when it exists — it REPLACES .gitignore
# rather than extending it. Every secret exclusion that .gitignore provides must
# therefore be repeated here. The first version of this file omitted them, and a
# dry run from a configured checkout packed .env, an APNS .p8 key, server.key,
# config/client-ca/ and private e2e config. Fixing a size problem introduced a
# credential-disclosure one.
#
# It also cannot simply mirror .gitignore: dist/ is gitignored but IS published,
# because package.json main points at dist/wsproxy.js.
#
# Before changing this file, check BOTH directions: that secrets are absent and
# that the artifact is still usable. Verifying only that the essentials survived
# is what let the first version through.

# --- Secrets and local credentials (mirrors .gitignore) ---
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.*.example
.envrc
!.envrc.example
*.key
*.p8
*.p12
*.pfx
cert.pem
privkey.pem
config/client-ca/
config/e2e/*.json
!config/e2e.example.json
config/attested-keys.json

# --- Agent runtime state and worktrees ---
# Excluded via .git/info/exclude for git, which npm never reads. Without this
# the tarball carried 263 entries and 98 MB of separate full checkouts.
.claude/

# --- Local artefacts ---
coverage/
.nyc_output/
logs/
*.log
**/.DS_Store

# --- Repository furniture a consumer does not need ---
.github/
docs/superpowers/
tests/
scripts/
.editorconfig
.prettierignore
.prettierrc.json
eslint.config.js
tsconfig.json
